{"auditVerdictAtHead":"pass","canonicalDigest":"sha256:52400e043a0bfb0cbb622813b3ab279ffd1bb2f3b9cfd9feccdc6a9d5c1f8438","canonicalizationVersion":"1","changeRequest":{"author":"buger","body":"Fixes #14052.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A summon now cancels a pending \"Do you want to uninstall …?\" question, the way its Cancel button does. Before, the question stayed on top of the new prompt with Uninstall preselected, so the Enter meant for the prompt uninstalled the app and cancelled the prompt.\n\n| | `quattro` `821ae58` | This PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| Delete on an app, then a prompt (`omarchy-menu-select`) is summoned | the question stays on top of the prompt | the prompt replaces the question |\n| Enter on that prompt | prompt cancelled (exit 1), **app uninstalled** | `apple`, exit 0; app still installed |\n| Same with `omarchy-menu-input` or `omarchy menu summon <route>` | app uninstalled | nothing uninstalled |\n| Delete, then Enter / Escape / Cancel on the question itself | uninstall / cancel / cancel | unchanged |\n\n### What changes\n\n`open(payloadJson)` is where every summon enters the menu, on its way to `openDmenu()` or `openRoute()` → `openExistingMenu()`. It now calls `cancelDelete()` when a question is pending:\n\n```qml\n// A summon replaces the rows an uninstall confirmation was raised for,\n// so the confirmation must not stay up to answer the new request.\nif (root.deleteConfirmOpen) root.cancelDelete()\n```\n\nUntil now the question was dropped on its own only in `onOpenedChanged` when the menu closed. A summon keeps `opened` true, so the question survived and kept taking every key.\n\n<details><summary>Why <code>cancelDelete()</code> and why in <code>open()</code></summary>\n\n- `cancelDelete()` is exactly what the Cancel button and Escape do. It also re-arms the pointer gate and refocuses the key catcher. The open paths do both anyway, so that repeat is harmless, and using it keeps \"dismiss the question\" in one place.\n- `open()` is the only caller of `openDmenu()` and `openRoute()`, so one line covers select, input and route summons. On the action-alias branch of `openRoute()` the menu closes anyway, and `onOpenedChanged` already cleared the question there.\n- Other paths that rebuild rows while the menu is open (JSONC reloads, `onAppsChanged`, providers) are not new requests, and `deleteTarget` holds the app id, so they can't retarget the uninstall. They are unchanged.\n\n</details>\n\nA 71-second narrated capture of the real shell under Quickshell, with keys from a virtual keyboard: upstream `quattro` `821ae58` uninstalls the app and cancels the prompt, and this branch's head `09bfcda` answers the prompt and keeps the app:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/de6daf44-a8a2-4025-b04c-bd02a952e6fa\n\n### How to check it\n\n- [x] new `test/shell.d/menu-uninstall-confirm-test.sh`: 10 `ok`; on `quattro` it fails at its first assertion\n- [x] every assertion that shows the bug fails on `quattro` by itself, not only the first one\n- [x] all menu tests still pass (`menu-test.sh` 127, `menu-guards` 18, `menu-plugin` 12, `menu-images` 6, `keybindings-menu` 16, `launcher-remove` 5)\n- [x] the full `./test/shell` run fails the same 17 files before and after (my Linux box isn't an Omarchy install); the new file passes\n- [x] in the real shell (summons over IPC, keys from `wtype`): the issue's scenario on `quattro` deletes the launcher; on this branch the prompt returns `apple` (`kiwi` for an input prompt) and the launcher stays. Escape, Cancel, Enter on the question itself, and closing the menu behave as before\n\n<details><summary>Commands</summary>\n\n```sh\nbash test/shell.d/menu-uninstall-confirm-test.sh\n\n# the same test against quattro's Menu.qml (expect: not ok - a select prompt summoned over an uninstall confirmation dismisses it)\ngit checkout 821ae58 -- shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml && bash test/shell.d/menu-uninstall-confirm-test.sh; git checkout HEAD -- shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml\n\nfor f in test/shell.d/menu*-test.sh test/shell.d/keybindings-menu-test.sh test/shell.d/launcher-remove-test.sh; do\n  bash \"$f\" >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo \"ok   $f\" || echo \"FAIL $f\"\ndone\n```\n\nFor the live check, follow the issue's steps (a throwaway launcher and a queued `omarchy-menu-select`).\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>About the test</summary>\n\nThe test runs the real `open`, `openRoute`, `openExistingMenu`, `openDmenu`, `requestDeleteSelected`, `cancelDelete`, `confirmDelete`, `cancel` and `finishRequest` bodies from `Menu.qml`. It also runs the real `Keys.onPressed` handler and `ConfirmDialog.handleKey` under `node:vm`, with the rows, the result writer and the app library stubbed. A regex on `Menu.qml` could only check that the line exists. This shows the behaviour: a summon dismisses the question, and the next Enter answers the prompt and removes nothing.\n\n- The cases are a select prompt, an input prompt and a route summon over a pending question. One more checks that Enter on the question itself still uninstalls.\n- A last assertion fails if the code writes a property the harness doesn't stub, so the harness can't silently drift from `Menu.qml`.\n- It is its own file so it doesn't collide with the many open PRs that append to `menu-test.sh`.\n\n</details>\n\n### What it could affect\n\nOnly the moment a summon arrives while the uninstall question is up. With no question pending, `open()` does what it did before. I test-merged this branch with each of the 91 open PRs that touch `Menu.qml`. It adds a conflict to none of them. Each merges exactly as it does with `quattro`, including the PRs that change `open()`: #13043, #13246, #12698, #8396, #8537 and #9056.\n\n---\n\n**Independent verification:** [the evidence for this PR](https://portal.reqproof.com/projects/omarchy/changes/pr/14054) comes from a full proof audit of `09bfcda` merged onto the current `quattro` (evaluated merge `5a62332`): test report 56 passed · 0 failed · 0 skipped, plus 7 tests observed by the behaviour comparison run: 7 passed.\n","bodyDigest":"sha256:0f3b8b4ba0c884dbfbf4a7002fe8d8e3cce694e58f829a55c8eddc213db674ce","bodyExcerpt":"Fixes #14052.","linkedIssues":["#14052"],"source":"explicit","title":"Keep an uninstall confirmation from answering the next menu summon"},"createdAt":"2026-10-02T17:43:15Z","decisionSummary":{"claimEvidence":[{"claim":"requirement_preserved","claimId":"requirement:SW-REQ-260922-3JG5","failed":0,"notRun":0,"obligations":[{"class":"boundary","failed":0,"observedVia":"SYS-REQ-260922-P708","passed":1,"skipped":0,"source":"inherited:SYS-REQ-260922-P708","status":"observed_pass","tests":1}],"passed":2,"requirementId":"SW-REQ-260922-3JG5","status":"observed_pass","unknown":0},{"claim":"requirement_preserved","claimId":"requirement:SW-REQ-260922-3T3F","failed":0,"notRun":0,"obligations":[{"class":"boundary","failed":0,"passed":2,"skipped":0,"source":"own","status":"observed_pass","tests":2},{"class":"error_handling","failed":0,"passed":2,"skipped":0,"source":"own","status":"observed_pass","tests":2},{"class":"input_domain","failed":0,"passed":1,"skipped":0,"source":"own","status":"observed_pass","tests":1}],"passed":3,"requirementId":"SW-REQ-260922-3T3F","status":"observed_pass","unknown":0},{"claim":"requirement_preserved","claimId":"requirement:SW-REQ-260922-3VTN","failed":0,"notRun":0,"obligations":[{"class":"error_handling","failed":0,"observedVia":"SYS-REQ-260922-X6Z5","passed":1,"skipped":0,"source":"inherited:SYS-REQ-260922-X6Z5","status":"observed_pass","tests":1},{"class":"input_domain","failed":0,"passed":0,"skipped":0,"source":"inherited:SYS-REQ-260922-X6Z5","status":"not_linked","tests":0}],"passed":2,"requirementId":"SW-REQ-260922-3VTN","status":"observed_pass","unknown":0},{"claim":"requirement_preserved","claimId":"requirement:SW-REQ-260922-4079","failed":0,"notRun":0,"obligations":[{"class":"error_handling","failed":0,"passed":0,"skipped":0,"source":"inherited:SYS-REQ-260922-47T8","status":"not_linked","tests":0},{"class